#43003
The Rim of the Valley~
   The forest opens suddenly at the edge of a great green valley.  Below
you, cupped between wooded slopes, lie meadows of silver grass, a
winding brook, an orchard heavy with golden fruit and, at the valley's
far end, a waterfall spilling down from the heights in a veil of mist.
Over it all hangs a strange stillness, as though the valley were waiting
for something.  A path winds down the slope, and the forest lies to the
south.
~
