#43014
The Pool of Reflections~
   A round pool lies here, perfectly still, its water so clear and dark
that it shows the sky above like a mirror, though the sky it shows is
not the one overhead.  When you lean over it, the face that looks back
at you is not quite your own: older, perhaps, or younger, or wearing an
expression you have never worn.  Just to the north three roads meet, and
the grove of threads lies to the west.
~
